WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.860
Every autumn, trees drop huge piles of leaves.

2
00:00:04.180 --> 00:00:06.560
A year later, many of them seem to be gone.

3
00:00:07.920 --> 00:00:08.920
Where did they go?

4
00:00:09.980 --> 00:00:13.000
Five sealed containers on a shelf will show your child.

5
00:00:16.033 --> 00:00:18.133
Set aside about twenty-five minutes.

6
00:00:19.193 --> 00:00:22.633
Then check the containers twice a week for three to four weeks.

7
00:00:23.813 --> 00:00:28.513
Your child practices looking closely, recording changes, and checking their guesses.

8
00:00:29.717 --> 00:00:32.917
Number five clear plastic tubs with tight lids.

9
00:00:34.117 --> 00:00:37.837
Put two or three spoonfuls of damp soil into each of the first four.

10
00:00:39.157 --> 00:00:40.497
Use one item per tub.

11
00:00:41.777 --> 00:00:46.277
Add half an apple slice, a dry leaf, bread, and a bottle cap, in that order.

12
00:00:47.300 --> 00:00:51.280
The fifth container gets the other half of the apple and no soil.

13
00:00:52.580 --> 00:00:54.760
Tape every lid shut, all the way around.

14
00:00:56.020 --> 00:00:58.140
Tell your child, 'These lids stay shut.

15
00:00:59.300 --> 00:01:01.660
We are detectives, so we look through the sides.'

16
00:01:02.733 --> 00:01:06.473
Before the first check, ask, 'Which one do you think will change first?'

17
00:01:07.153 --> 00:01:08.233
Write down the guess together.

18
00:01:09.553 --> 00:01:12.573
Have your child draw what each container looks like on day one.

19
00:01:13.567 --> 00:01:15.247
Now a question for you.

20
00:01:16.347 --> 00:01:20.387
After two weeks on a shelf, which containers do you predict will look different?

21
00:01:21.627 --> 00:01:23.627
And which one will look exactly the same?

22
00:01:29.150 --> 00:01:32.430
Bread often grows fuzzy mold within one to two weeks.

23
00:01:33.690 --> 00:01:36.810
Both apples usually rot, even the one with no soil.

24
00:01:38.410 --> 00:01:40.310
Mold spores are in the air and on the fruit.

25
00:01:41.590 --> 00:01:43.430
The leaf may barely change in a month.

26
00:01:44.433 --> 00:01:46.953
The bottle cap can look the same at the end.

27
00:01:48.213 --> 00:01:51.013
Most decomposers cannot use plastic as food.

28
00:01:52.453 --> 00:01:54.293
Decomposers break down dead things.

29
00:01:55.533 --> 00:01:59.153
Here, the main ones are tiny living things like bacteria and mold.

30
00:02:00.267 --> 00:02:03.807
Each time you look, ask, 'What is different since last time?'

31
00:02:04.647 --> 00:02:07.027
Compare the apple in soil with the apple on its own.

32
00:02:08.287 --> 00:02:09.867
At the end, line up the drawings.

33
00:02:11.267 --> 00:02:15.947
Use them to check the starting guess and sort fast, slow, and unchanged results.

34
00:02:17.050 --> 00:02:19.010
You set up and seal every tub.

35
00:02:20.310 --> 00:02:22.450
Keep the tubs on a shelf out of direct sun.

36
00:02:23.730 --> 00:02:25.850
Stay with your child and look through the sides.

37
00:02:27.170 --> 00:02:29.630
Nobody opens, sniffs, or shakes a tub.

38
00:02:31.210 --> 00:02:33.410
Mold spores can set off allergies and asthma.

39
00:02:34.770 --> 00:02:39.870
Anyone with asthma, a mold allergy, or a weakened immune system should leave the

40
00:02:39.870 --> 00:02:43.570
containers alone. Wash hands after each check.

41
00:02:44.567 --> 00:02:49.807
A bottle cap, foil ball, or other small piece is a choking risk for children under

42
00:02:49.807 --> 00:02:52.947
four. Keep small pieces out of reach.

43
00:02:54.347 --> 00:02:56.247
Call nine one one if a child is choking.

44
00:02:57.587 --> 00:03:00.187
Never taste the leaf or any food used here.

45
00:03:01.007 --> 00:03:04.847
At the end, bag the sealed tubs and put them in the outdoor trash.

46
00:03:05.867 --> 00:03:07.947
So where did all those autumn leaves go?

47
00:03:09.527 --> 00:03:13.027
Tiny living things ate them, slowly, and returned the bits to the soil.

48
00:03:14.327 --> 00:03:16.047
New plants use those bits to grow.
